# Context for backend/Dockerfile.prod is the repo root (it needs backend/ AND templates/app-skeleton).
# Allowlist: everything is excluded, then the two trees are let back in, then junk inside them is
# excluded again. Keeps the context to source only — no node_modules, venvs or build output.
*
!backend
!templates/app-skeleton
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/dist
**/coverage
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
# Real secrets only — the skeleton ships .env.example files the generated app needs.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
backend/tests
